# Bot1 has Dauthi Voidwalker ("if a card would be put into an opponent's graveyard from anywhere, instead exile it with a
# void counter on it") out on turn 1. On turn 2 Bot2 discards Basking Rootwalla and a Mountain to Faithless Looting. Two
# replacements apply to the Rootwalla's discard, madness (CR 702.35a) and the Voidwalker's; Bot2, the card's owner and
# the affected player, orders them (CR 616.1), not the Voidwalker's controller. Bot2 takes madness first, so the card is
# exiled without a void counter and Bot2 casts it for {0} (the Voidwalker ruling: madness still works). The Mountain and
# the Looting are exiled with void counters.

[Bot1 Deck]
Swamp
Mox Jet
Dauthi Voidwalker
Swamp x17

[Bot2 Deck]
Mountain
Faithless Looting
Basking Rootwalla
Mountain
Mountain x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Swamp.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Swamp.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Dauthi Voidwalker.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot2.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Faithless Looting.Cast
Bot2.Choose(Basking Rootwalla; Mountain)
Bot2.Replace(madness)
? Stack.Count = 1
Bot2.Accept

[Expect]
Turn = 2
Stack.Count = 0
Bot2.Battlefield = Mountain; Basking Rootwalla
Bot2.Graveyard.Count = 0
Exile = Faithless Looting; Mountain
